{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1453229-expanding-improving-the-beast-courts-and-ahadi-and-more","id":1453229,"title":"Expanding/Improving the Beast Courts and Ahadi and more","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-22T19:45:54-07:00","id":1453229,"title":"Expanding/Improving the Beast Courts and Ahadi and more","content":"Simply put I love the idea of systems that really let multi Fera teams work together, but the Beast Courts feel off in a way I cant quite place and the Ahadi are very sparse and Localized to a single place in their offerings.<br /> <br /> This is a thread to pitch offerings on how to Expand and Improve these factions and come up with Equivalents in other locations and eras.<br /> <br /> On my end I've Recently come up with 3 additional concepts<br /> <br /> The first is the Simplest, informal Fera Packs that simply manage to work together, Called Menageries.<br /> <br /> The Second is based on my earlier Concept for a Cyberdog's Successor Faction, under the working title of the HardWare Beasts<br /> <br /> the most fleshed out is one that seems a bit obvious honestly Based around South and Meso American cultures, the Nagual, with lots of Olmec, Mayan, Inca and Aztec Styling to them, being a faction that actually broke apart During the Second War of Rage, and is in the process of being Re-founded and having much of its culture activly rediscovered by people divided from their ancestors by many generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T21:28:50-07:00","id":1453240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazyjabberwock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1453229-expanding-improving-the-beast-courts-and-ahadi-and-more#post1453229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the Ahadi are very sparse and Localized to a single place in their offerings.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels a bit unfair as of W20. The Ahadi cover a territory the size of the USA, India, and China combined, with a human population of over a billion people with a huge variety of cultures within it. Reducing it to &quot;a single place&quot; feels... off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first is the Simplest, informal Fera Packs that simply manage to work together, Called Menageries. </div> </div> </div>I think the big thing to work on here? Why. If it's going to be more than just temporary alliances, there needs to be something keeping it going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the most fleshed out is one that seems a bit obvious honestly Based around South and Meso American cultures, the Nagual, with lots of Olmec, Mayan, Inca and Aztec Styling to them, being a faction that actually broke apart During the Second War of Rage, and is in the process of being Re-founded and having much of its culture activly rediscovered by people divided from their ancestors by many generations. </div> </div> </div>I think this is the strongest one. You have the Amazon War as a good impetus to push the local Fera to (re-)create their own organization to deal with the incursions of Garou that want to dictate how the area is run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T21:59:37-07:00","id":1453242,"title":"","content":"Menageries were meant to be very loose, just a simple basic means of letting Fera and Garou mixed groups work together more cleanly under a shared moniker, but I'm open to some ideas to turn it into something more solid.<br /> <br /> And I'll admit, the Ahadi was unfair and the Beast Courts was more an attempt to offer an opening for people who had Critiques for them, I'm still researching them myself and so cant fully form an opinion on them. <br /> <br /> The Nagual faction was inspired partially by the fact that lots of compatible Totem spirits already exist for such a group with little to no tweaking, and I liked the idea of it having two distinct founding both before and after the second war of rage.<br /> <br /> Totems I found are here<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Citlacoatl\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Citlacoatl</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bird_of_Paradise_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bird_of_Paradise_(WTA</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Xochipilli\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Xochipilli</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Coatimundi\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Coatimundi</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tezcatlipoca_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tezcatlipoca_(WTA</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Waterfall_(Totem\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Waterfall_(Totem</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Maize_(Totem\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Maize_(Totem</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Frog_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Frog_(WTA</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Quetzal_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Quetzal_(WTA</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bat_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bat_(WTA</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anaconda\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anaconda</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hummingbird\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hummingbird</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jaguar\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jaguar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Panther_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Panther_(WTA</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Panthesilea\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Panthesilea</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Chameleon_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Chameleon_(WTA</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Corn_Maiden\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Corn_Maiden</a><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dragonfly_(WTA\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dragonfly_(WTA</a>)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T22:13:57-07:00","id":1453243,"title":"","content":"I have to redo this whole damn post because I some how messed up on the posting reply part.<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree, I was a little unfair to the Ahadi and Beast Courts and was mostly doing it to open the door to Critique better then mine could be from others who have read more on them, as I'm still in the learning process, but have heard criticisms to them before that I wanted to let people brooch on this thread, the intention is to pitch ways they can be better afterall.<br /> <br /> The Nagual are genuinely the one I'm proudest of in terms of Concepts as it creates a contrast to both the Long lived Beast Courts and the Fresh and Idealistic Ahadi, being an example of such Cooperation that Failed once already and needs to be activly rediscovered by people divided from the last ones to actually be part of it by a good many generations. Themes of Grudges and Forgiveness, of learning from the failings and successes of the past, plus while we could always make some new Totems to go with them, the Region has a LOT of Totem Spirits already quite ready for them, needing little to no tweaking to suit the faction. <br /> <br /> The Menageries was meant to be as simple as possible, a no Frills approach to Fera (Garou Included) working in a team under a unified name, I'm open to suggestens to make this concept a more Solid Thing in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T04:13:54-07:00","id":1453258,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest problem with South and Central America is how much the canon stuff ruins diversity in Fera there. Despite the massive biodiversity in the area, the books are written so that so many Fera aren't present there natively (either naturally or any more). Unless you're willing to do some serious retconing of the setting, there's an annoying lack of history to tie into as a middle ground between the Beast Courts and the Ahadi.<br /> <br /> The whole Menagerie concept either needs a major setting overhaul if you're going to make them relatively common, or if you want something special and rare but more than just a few Fera of different types cooperating out of mutual self-interest, you need to do something like Phoenix and the Silver Pack: a Totem that basically exists just to form these special groups and guide them to some major service towards Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:15:38-07:00","id":1453284,"title":"","content":"In large part the stuff that feels &quot;off&quot; is how terribly functional these multi-fera organizations work in the context of werewolf's Tribalism. Werewolves hate other werewolves, and yet a pan-african alliance is treated with so much optimism (They're not flawless, clearly, I just expect them to be more flawed) while the Beast courts carry a lot of Asian superiority connotations. This might be more because I'm reading mostly W20 material and W20 material is a lot more optimistic about people working together than 1/2e, but I feel like a lot more flaws needed to be added; an undercurrent of speciesism, nepotism, princes fighting for a hereditary possition, officials abusing power; &quot;this king/You Dare/You made me draw my sword/refuse a toast only to drink a forfeit/playing pig to eat the tiger; all that stuff common in historical/fantastical asian dramas is so terribly absent from the Beast courts. As creatures of Rage, some degree of dysfunction needs to be established to control their society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T11:58:53-07:00","id":1453304,"title":"","content":"On the Menageries I'm brainstorming a Spirit Brood Headed by a Totem called Echidna (named more for the mythical Mother of Monsters and Daughter of Gaia then the Monotrime) who's mostly focused on trying to heal relations one pack at a time then in big Pushes.<br /> <br /> The Ahadi's Optomism feels to me like an in universe thing from what I've read, and earned after pulling a legitimately impressive victory over Blacktooth, but there should be emphasis on how potentially fragile their movement should be, Africa is a big place with lots of threats, Set's Curse and Entirely too many Vampires in Egypt, Bane Mummies, Pentex Agents setting to fill the power vaccume and Directing Kerasi Mockeries to try and manipulate, not to Mention the Nagah having the potential to decide to pull the plug on them for compromising the sacred secret and the Fact that Ananasi who don't actually have any true loyalty being let into their circles and who would on the barest Command of Ananansa, betray them all in an instant. Their Flaw isn't in their ideals or what they are, its in how little they've safeguarded what they've made.<br /> <br /> For the Beast Courts, reading more, It is alarming how little from the same martial arts Flicks, Samurai Flicks and Anime that almost surely inspired the courts has been used to flesh out their flaws. Any half decent Samurai story can show stories of Courtly Rivalries, Atrocities upon peasants, and Honor Codes being used as an excuse for terrible Actions or Inaction. The Zhong Lung Could Easily be likened to the Imperial Nobility during the warring states period, Gazing so hard into often nonexistent Navels that they forget to spend any time being leader's to their people. and thats just the Japanese Inspired part, There's also ideas that could be taken from Mongolia, China, India, the Philippines, The Himalayas, plenty of spotty history that can be brought in or used as inspiration, the Courts are Old and should have a History unto themselves. <br /> <br /> The Nagual, I'm Borderline willing to use in a Flat out re-write of the Canon South American stuff, much of which was originally written when the Fera were being treated as little more then C List support characters as Opposed to Supporting Protagonists, the Amazon War itself makes sense and the Second War of Rage also has potential. The Blank Spots Can potentially also serve well as a free canvas to fill in if needed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T04:24:51-07:00","id":1454065,"title":"","content":"Theres a whole bunch of Brazil-based books written by locals on the ST Vault for WtA that may be of use to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In my own games I had a somewhat similar arrangement existing in Australia/Oceania pre-Garou Nation arrival..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T15:23:58-07:00","id":1454101,"title":"","content":"Oh? tell me about it, I'd love to see more ideas, and how do I narrow to just Brazil based books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T20:32:59-07:00","id":1454170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazyjabberwock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1453229-expanding-improving-the-beast-courts-and-ahadi-and-more?p=1454101#post1454101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? tell me about it, I'd love to see more ideas, and how do I narrow to just Brazil based books?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Pedro%20Ribeiro%20Nogueira\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/site-logo-redesignd.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Pedro%20Ribeiro%20Nogueira\" target=\"_blank\"> Storytellers Vault - </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Pedro%20Ribeiro%20Nogueira\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Pedro%20Ribeiro%20Nogueira </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> , wot pdf, nwod pdf, download wod, white wolf, ww, nwod, vtm, mta, mage the ascension, world of darkness </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T21:52:10-07:00","id":1454173,"title":"","content":"thanks man, I'll have a look over the week<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T06:43:28-07:00","id":1457896,"title":"","content":"The lack of conflict on the Beast Courts is partly tied to how East Asia (mostly with the exception of Russia) is generally treated in WoD, with local politics setting the conflicts far more than rigid splat lines. The problem is that on most of them the &quot;Asian Splats&quot; are actually very different from the European ones, while the Fera are theoretically the same, and that makes the work hard and, in my opinion, contrived. Especially on Kumo (Rokea too, but they're so inane and nonsensical on default that the nonsensical change actually makes for a better experience).<br /> <br /> My opinion is that your first idea can work well if you dare to update the setting on your own to a proper &quot;20 years later&quot; state. After the experience of the Ahadi it isn't that hard to think that contact between the Fera increased over the past years, enough for mixed groups being a thing, even if rare. By the Time of Judgement books it was already starting to feel less and less credible that the Fera had no contact at all, even with the world going nuts around them. Their societies may still be at odds, but a few mixed groups here and there should be a thing already. I don't think they need a moniker, though.<br /> <br /> I also thought your Nagual idea interesting, and although I didn't look at those books Damian May linked yet, I can help you with any Brazilian-based part of it if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}